# ImageJ1 style registration.
#
# The SciJava @Plugin annotations alone put the smFRET menu in the trailing section of the
# Plugins menu, after the separator that follows "Volume Viewer", because that is where
# imagej-legacy appends ImageJ2 commands. Menu weights cannot move it across that separator.
# Registering here as well puts it in the main plugins section instead, alongside 3D Viewer,
# TurboReg and the rest.
#
# The classes below are SciJava Commands, not ij.plugin.PlugIn implementations. Fiji's legacy
# patcher dispatches these entries into the SciJava command service anyway, so the parameter
# dialogs are still generated - verified by running "smFRET Trace Histograms" from this entry.
#
# IMPORTANT: in Fiji the order of the entries in THIS file determines the order of the items
# within the smFRET submenu. The @Menu weights in the source files do not - they are the
# SciJava side declaration and only take effect where the legacy layer is not in play. To
# reorder the menu, reorder these lines.
#
# Format: <menu path>, "<label>", <class>

Plugins>smFRET, "smFRET Channel Mapping", smFRETChannelMapper
Plugins>smFRET, "smFRET Spot Finder", smFRETSpotFinder
Plugins>smFRET, "smFRET Time Traces", smFRETAnalyzer
Plugins>smFRET, "smFRET Trace Histograms", smFRETTraceHistogram
